---
interface Props {
  toolName: string;
}

const { toolName } = Astro.props;
---

<section class="seo-content-section container-stripe">
  <div class="seo-content-wrapper">
    <h2>How to Remove Passwords from PDFs Offline</h2>
    <p class="seo-p">
      Removing a password or permission lock from a PDF document usually means uploading your highly sensitive financial or legal documents to a third-party server. Our <strong>Remove Password from PDF</strong> tool changes the paradigm. By leveraging WebAssembly, we securely unlock and decrypt your PDF documents entirely within your local browser.
    </p>

    <div class="seo-grid">
      <div class="seo-card">
        <h3>100% Client-Side Decryption</h3>
        <p class="seo-p">
          We utilize an enterprise-grade QPDF WebAssembly engine that runs locally on your device. Your sensitive passwords and confidential documents never leave your computer, ensuring absolute privacy.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="seo-card">
        <h3>Lossless Quality</h3>
        <p class="seo-p">
          Unlike other offline tools that flatten or rasterize your PDF into an image (destroying text selection and links), our tool manipulates the raw PDF structure. Text, vector graphics, and forms remain perfectly intact.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="seo-card">
        <h3>Automatic Permission Unlocking</h3>
        <p class="seo-p">
          If your PDF only has an "owner" password (restricting printing or copying), you don't even need to enter a password. Our tool automatically detects and strips these restrictions silently in the background.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="seo-faq">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h4>Is this really safe for tax documents and bank statements?</h4>
        <p class="seo-p">
          Yes. Because the decryption engine is downloaded to your browser and runs locally in your RAM, there is zero risk of your files being intercepted or stored on a remote server. You can even disconnect from the internet before unlocking the file.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h4>Why do I need to enter a password for some files but not others?</h4>
        <p class="seo-p">
          PDFs have two types of passwords. "User passwords" encrypt the entire document and require the password to even open it. "Owner passwords" only restrict permissions like printing. Our tool can automatically bypass owner restrictions, but requires the password to decrypt user-locked files.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h4>Will my unlocked PDF look identical?</h4>
        <p class="seo-p">
          Absolutely. The decryption process is 100% mathematically lossless. All fonts, images, hyperlinks, and vector data are preserved exactly as they were in the original document.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .seo-content-section {
    padding: 64px 24px;
    background: var(--color-surface-1);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .seo-content-wrapper {
    max-width: 860px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  h3 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  h4 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .seo-p {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-ink-2);
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }

  .seo-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
    gap: 24px;
    margin: 48px 0;
  }

  .seo-card {
    background: var(--color-surface-2);
    padding: 32px;
    border-radius: 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .seo-card .seo-p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .seo-faq {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 24px;
    margin-top: 32px;
  }

  .faq-item {
    background: var(--color-surface-2);
    padding: 24px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .faq-item .seo-p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>
